WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.414 --> 00:00:11.485
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:12.052 --> 00:00:13.387
[turret beeping]

00:00:13.387 --> 00:00:15.856
[turret beeping]
This thing is still beeping.

00:00:15.856 --> 00:00:19.226
[turret beeping]
It won't stop.  The others stopped.

00:00:19.226 --> 00:00:21.128
[turret beeping]
That doesn't bother so much as the fact

00:00:21.128 --> 00:00:23.230
[turret beeping]
that it sprays automatic gunfire at me

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.264
[turret beeping]
when it beeps.

00:00:24.264 --> 00:00:25.966
[turret beeping]
I can't live with that.

00:00:25.966 --> 00:00:27.501
[turret beeping]
Like, literally.

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:29.336
[turret beeping]
I don't know, maybe I can outrun it.

00:00:29.336 --> 00:00:30.604
[turret beeping]
I'm a track star.

00:00:30.604 --> 00:00:31.638
[turret beeping]
I'm amazing.

00:00:31.638 --> 00:00:32.606
[turret beeping]
I'm gonna do it.

00:00:32.606 --> 00:00:33.073
[turret beeping]
Pew!

00:00:33.073 --> 00:00:34.141
[turret firing]

00:00:34.141 --> 00:00:35.409
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:00:35.409 --> 00:00:36.176
That worked!

00:00:36.176 --> 00:00:39.446
And you can't chase me because
you don't have any legs!

00:00:39.446 --> 00:00:41.448
La la la la!

00:00:41.448 --> 00:00:43.784
At least, I don't think it does.

00:00:43.784 --> 00:00:45.886
No, that would require
gyroscopes

00:00:45.886 --> 00:00:48.455
and it would look more
like the Terminator, or something.

00:00:48.455 --> 00:00:51.458
Which would be sweet, but I
don't want that after me.

00:00:51.458 --> 00:00:53.026
Oh, no, another soldier.

00:00:53.026 --> 00:00:54.261
Did he see me?

00:00:54.728 --> 00:00:56.897
Maybe not.

00:00:56.897 --> 00:00:58.098
Yes!  Dammit...

00:00:58.098 --> 00:00:59.900
That answers that question.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:03.170
Why does everyone here insist on
doing things the hard way?

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:05.005
They should be doing things my way.

00:01:06.006 --> 00:01:07.641
Okay, fine!  We'll do it your way!

00:01:09.042 --> 00:01:10.944
There!  Are you happy now?!

00:01:11.578 --> 00:01:13.547
Oh, guess not!

00:01:13.547 --> 00:01:16.116
Y'know, some people just create
their own problems.

00:01:16.116 --> 00:01:17.451
And you're one of them.

00:01:17.451 --> 00:01:18.752
And, see, look at this.

00:01:18.752 --> 00:01:20.687
I've never had any military training

00:01:20.687 --> 00:01:23.857
so I don't know the correct
procedure for these things.

00:01:23.857 --> 00:01:27.027
But, if I saw my buddy run
around the corner then get shot,

00:01:27.027 --> 00:01:31.031
then I saw my next buddy run around
the same corner and get shot,

00:01:31.031 --> 00:01:33.500
I don't think I'd run around
that same corner.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.870
But, I use discretion.  You're not allowed
to have that in the military.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.271
WHAT THE HELL?!

00:01:39.139 --> 00:01:41.241
YOU CAN'T DO THAT!

00:01:41.241 --> 00:01:42.876
I'm an American!

00:01:42.876 --> 00:01:45.779
God dammit, it's like, what's the point
of being an honest citizen

00:01:45.779 --> 00:01:47.881
if I'm going to get shot at anyway?

00:01:47.881 --> 00:01:49.149
Hello?

00:01:49.149 --> 00:01:49.750
No...

00:01:50.884 --> 00:01:52.753
This is so unproductive.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:55.522
You fell for that trick again!

00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:58.592
And again...

00:01:58.592 --> 00:02:01.862
I guess you guys are
learn-from-experience types.

00:02:01.862 --> 00:02:04.064
Though, that only gets you so far.

00:02:04.064 --> 00:02:06.466
I bet you guys suck as chess.

00:02:06.466 --> 00:02:09.603
Just keep doing the same thing
until you're all dead.

00:02:09.603 --> 00:02:11.438
You could never do my job.

00:02:12.072 --> 00:02:12.439
Ah!

00:02:13.507 --> 00:02:15.542
Man, if I get indicted once I leave here,

00:02:15.542 --> 00:02:18.345
this is getting harder
and harder to explain.

00:02:18.345 --> 00:02:21.648
I don't think anyone's going to buy
a few dozen counts of self-defense

00:02:21.648 --> 00:02:23.283
with a submachine gun.

00:02:23.283 --> 00:02:25.986
I think there's kind of an
unspoken rule in our society

00:02:25.986 --> 00:02:29.656
that if this many people are trying
to kill you, you're supposed to be dead.

00:02:29.656 --> 00:02:31.258
I need to talk to an attorney.

00:02:31.258 --> 00:02:33.393
Maybe there's some sort of Rambo clause.

00:02:33.393 --> 00:02:36.463
But, wait, Rambo goes to prison
after the first movie.

00:02:36.463 --> 00:02:37.264
Fuck.

00:02:37.264 --> 00:02:38.098
What's this do?

00:02:39.032 --> 00:02:39.466
Oh.

00:02:39.933 --> 00:02:40.400
Well.

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:41.301
Shoot.

00:02:41.735 --> 00:02:44.070
Um, I'm not jumping this.

00:02:44.838 --> 00:02:46.573
Why are the controls on and off?

00:02:46.573 --> 00:02:48.575
They should be up and d--
oh, there it goes.

00:02:49.409 --> 00:02:51.578
Okay, so do I just hit it real quick?

00:02:51.578 --> 00:02:53.380
Well, there's only one button.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:55.048
All right, one, two, three--GO!

00:02:55.582 --> 00:02:56.650
Jesus!

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.753
This is the complete opposite of
handicapped-accessible.

00:02:59.753 --> 00:03:01.555
Wait, what's with all these lasers?

00:03:01.555 --> 00:03:03.356
Okay, you I know what to do with.

00:03:04.324 --> 00:03:06.226
Well, that's one problem solved.

00:03:06.226 --> 00:03:08.495
Okay, let's try this again.

00:03:08.495 --> 00:03:10.063
Byzantine lift...

00:03:10.764 --> 00:03:12.899
One...two...three...GO!

00:03:14.034 --> 00:03:14.501
God!

00:03:15.402 --> 00:03:17.137
Okay, get off the lift.

00:03:17.137 --> 00:03:19.139
That's the first step...

00:03:19.139 --> 00:03:21.441
...to...a better life.

00:03:21.441 --> 00:03:23.577
I don't know what the
hell I'm talking about.

00:03:23.577 --> 00:03:25.712
Lasers!  Lasers...

00:03:25.712 --> 00:03:29.249
Nothing good ever happens with
lasers around here.

00:03:29.249 --> 00:03:32.085
So, I'm just gonna not deal with that.

00:03:32.085 --> 00:03:34.621
That's my favorite
solution to any problem.

00:03:34.621 --> 00:03:37.958
It's like the classic debate of why
measuring the position of an electron

00:03:37.958 --> 00:03:40.260
changes its momentum and vice versa.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:43.630
The only correct answer is to
get drunk and set fire to things.

00:03:44.431 --> 00:03:46.366
Oh, boy.  More of you.

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:49.936
These are like squeak toys from hell.

00:03:51.705 --> 00:03:53.974
Actually, if it wasn't for that
shockwave thing they do,

00:03:53.974 --> 00:03:55.675
they could be useful for a new sport.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:00.447
We could just get a stadium, then release
a dozen of them out onto the field,

00:04:00.447 --> 00:04:03.917
then get a bunch soccer players to run
out there and kick them all to death.

00:04:03.917 --> 00:04:06.353
The team that kills the most wins.

00:04:06.353 --> 00:04:08.822
Ah-ha!  "Power Generator".

00:04:08.822 --> 00:04:12.459
Hm, I guess we would need an odd number
of them to reduce the number of draws.

00:04:12.459 --> 00:04:13.560
But there's always the problem of

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.763
what if two opposing teams kill
one at the same time?

00:04:16.763 --> 00:04:19.399
You know, what might work better
is to kill them first,

00:04:19.399 --> 00:04:23.670
then kick their bodies into the field
goals and count THOSE as the points.

00:04:24.571 --> 00:04:28.108
And if you kick it too early and one's
still alive, then that's a penalty point.

00:04:28.108 --> 00:04:29.309
Yeah, this has potential.

00:04:29.309 --> 00:04:32.012
I'm going to stop by the patent
office once I get out of here.

00:04:32.012 --> 00:04:35.015
Okay, electricity.  Kind of scary...

00:04:35.015 --> 00:04:36.116
...with the arcs.

00:04:37.484 --> 00:04:39.886
Yeah, whether it's particle or a
wave doesn't really matter.

00:04:39.886 --> 00:04:41.488
It'll still kill you.

00:04:41.488 --> 00:04:43.256
Well, this looks like the place.

00:04:43.256 --> 00:04:44.057
Let's go.

00:04:44.057 --> 00:04:44.591
[panel buzzes]

00:04:45.592 --> 00:04:47.160
Y'know, if I'd have known
this thing was broken,

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.963
I could've saved myself the trouble
of killing all those people.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:51.531
Okay, mad dash!

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:56.770
Well, at least I'm okay.  That's
all history needs to remember.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.038
Still, this is ridiculous.

00:04:58.038 --> 00:05:01.074
The soldiers should be fixing
the generator, not me.

00:05:01.074 --> 00:05:03.910
I'm doing their job, again!

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:07.080
First, I'm killing everyone for
them, now I'm playing engineer.

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:12.686
You don't even have a job!
You're a vagrant.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:17.190
This place reminds me of the basement of
my old apartment that got flooded b--

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:18.925
Uck.  Worms.

00:05:18.925 --> 00:05:21.995
...got flooded because I did a
cannonball to the bathtub...

00:05:21.995 --> 00:05:24.297
..caused it to collapse into the floor...

00:05:24.898 --> 00:05:25.432
Dammit.

00:05:26.099 --> 00:05:27.167
Stupid worms.

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:29.002
I'm leaving!

00:05:29.002 --> 00:05:31.705
Alright, it's moving.
Mission accomplished.

00:05:31.705 --> 00:05:33.940
If any of these worms get in my
hair, I swear to God,

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:35.475
I'm just going to freak out.

00:05:35.475 --> 00:05:38.912
Yeah, worms get in my hair, the power
fails, and all the lights go out.

00:05:38.912 --> 00:05:41.314
Then some old guy with a raspy
voice starts laughing

00:05:41.314 --> 00:05:42.849
and poking me with a stick.

00:05:42.849 --> 00:05:45.218
That would complete the experience.

00:05:45.218 --> 00:05:47.554
Why was all this water down here anyway?

00:05:47.554 --> 00:05:50.223
I'm in the middle of
the desert in New Mexico.

00:05:50.223 --> 00:05:53.126
Does that mean I'm below the water table?

00:05:53.126 --> 00:05:57.297
If so, good God!
How deep am I right now?

00:05:57.297 --> 00:06:00.867
Okay, I'm going to give this
one more shot, then...

00:06:00.867 --> 00:06:02.335
I don't now what I'm going to do.

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:06.873
Work, you antiquated piece of crap.

00:06:06.873 --> 00:06:08.675
Hey, that did it!

00:06:08.675 --> 00:06:12.178
Now I can power up the train and
leave like--what was that?

00:06:13.213 --> 00:06:16.049
Oh, my...that's bad.

00:06:16.049 --> 00:06:20.220
That must be a fuckton of
voltage to jump like that.

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.155
Maybe I can--NYAAAH!

00:06:22.789 --> 00:06:23.456
God.

00:06:23.857 --> 00:06:26.793
Yeah, I can't say wearing a suit
covered in plate metal

00:06:26.793 --> 00:06:29.362
inspires confidence if that had hit me.

00:06:29.362 --> 00:06:32.632
I mean, Jesus, most people
hit by lightning survive,

00:06:32.632 --> 00:06:36.336
but that's because they're wearing rubber
shoes and you can see where it exits.

00:06:36.336 --> 00:06:38.605
But, if that hit me right now,

00:06:38.605 --> 00:06:42.442
the current would roll around in my
body and exit through the top.

00:06:42.442 --> 00:06:47.280
My head would blow up like a
baked potato wrapped in tinfoil.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.916
It would pop off like a Pez container.

00:06:49.916 --> 00:06:52.185
I think I need to go the other way.

00:06:52.185 --> 00:06:55.822
Actually, if it wasn't me, it would be
cool to watch if you got that on film.

00:06:55.822 --> 00:06:58.992
Their hair might catch on fire and it
might look like that scene from Scanners,

00:06:58.992 --> 00:07:00.827
except this would be the real thing.

00:07:00.827 --> 00:07:03.630
Then you could sell it as a snuff film
and make a bundle of money.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:04.664
I know buyers.

00:07:05.365 --> 00:07:06.733
Oh, give me a break!

00:07:06.733 --> 00:07:08.001
[explosion]

00:07:08.001 --> 00:07:10.103
Yeah, I should've known better.
I fixed the generator.

00:07:10.103 --> 00:07:11.871
Maybe now they need to come in and break it.

00:07:12.305 --> 00:07:16.209
Uh oh!  Everything's working fine!
Better call in the military!

00:07:16.209 --> 00:07:17.210
Wait, where did they go?

00:07:17.677 --> 00:07:19.345
I DIDN'T IMAGINE THEM!

00:07:19.846 --> 00:07:22.115
Hey, there's less lasers now.

00:07:22.115 --> 00:07:24.017
There's scorch marks.

00:07:24.017 --> 00:07:25.185
They're gone.

00:07:25.185 --> 00:07:28.855
Holy shit!  These were tripmines!

00:07:28.855 --> 00:07:30.957
I could've died!

00:07:30.957 --> 00:07:32.492
Well, glad I didn't touch them.

00:07:33.126 --> 00:07:34.561
How am I going to get back up?

00:07:36.429 --> 00:07:38.398
I brush with Death so often,

00:07:38.398 --> 00:07:40.398
I should start giving him
high-fives when I pass.

